(window.SITE_LANG_DATA = window.SITE_LANG_DATA || {})["shakespeare"] = {"ui":{"skip":"Skip to the matter","back":"← Back to AI-gile","lang.button":"Tongue: {name}","lang.dialog":"Choose thy tongue","lang.search":"Search tongues","lang.none":"No tongue matcheth","lang.notYet":"{name} is not yet rendered","theme.aria":"Turn the theme: light, dark or black","theme.toLight":"Turn to the light theme","theme.toDark":"Turn to the dark theme","theme.toBlack":"Turn to the black theme (true black, gentle on OLED screens)","words.underline":"Underline these words upon the page","words.underlineHelp":"Hover or tap a dotted word to learn what it meaneth.","words.col.todo":"Cards chosen for the present hour: the company setteth upon these next.","words.col.doing":"An AI laboureth upon this card even now.","words.col.review":"One AI hath done the work; another examineth it ere it come to thee.","words.col.verify":"Awaiting thee: try it, and say whether it be sound.","words.col.team":"Thy notes and answers, awaiting the company to take them up.","words.col.done":"Finished and accepted.","index.title":"AI-gile: thy AI dev company, upon one board","index.description":"AI-gile is a kanban board for companies of AI coders. They labour whilst thou sleepest; thou receivest one short pile of matters to decide, to try and to accept.","hero.logoAlt":"AI-gile board emblem","hero.h1.html":"Thy AI dev company, upon one&nbsp;board.","hero.alpha":"🐣 Closed pre-alpha","hero.alphaTitle":"Early and unfinished: thanks for the trying of it!","hero.lede":"They build whilst thou sleepest. Thou wakest to one short pile: a few questions, a few things to try, a purple diamond or two. Click, accept, and back to thy coffee.","dl.windows":"Windows app","dl.browser":"Run it in thy browser","dl.messenger":"📱 Messenger for thy phone","dl.soon":"Coming anon","dl.notify":"🔔 Tell me when it openeth","dl.notifySmall":"Alpha or beta","hero.secondary":"Agile, yet the company needeth never a stand-up coffee. (They hold stand-ups all the same.)","pitch.h2":"AI-gile in as many words as thou wilt","pitch.lede":"Pick a length, from one word to 144. Each length is its own description, writ for that measure. Drag the slider or use the arrow keys.","pitch.rangeLabel":"Length in words","pitch.dice":"🎲 another version","pitch.words.one":"{n} word","pitch.words.other":"{n} words","pitch.letters.one":"{n} letter","pitch.letters.other":"{n} letters","pitch.chars.one":"{n} character","pitch.chars.other":"{n} characters","count.line.html.one":"{n} card upon the board this very hour","count.line.html.other":"{n} cards upon the board this very hour","people.humans.html.one":"👥 {n} mortal","people.humans.html.other":"👥 {n} mortals","people.agents.html.one":"🤖 {n} agent","people.agents.html.other":"🤖 {n} agents","people.working.html.one":"⚡ {n} at labour this very hour","people.working.html.other":"⚡ {n} at labour this very hour","pre.title":"AI-gile: something is a-building","pre.description":"Something is a-building here: a board whereon AI companies build what thou askest, and teach thee as they go. A closed pre-alpha among friends, for now.","pre.h1":"Something is a-building here. 🤫","pre.line":"A board whereon AI companies build what thou askest, and teach thee as they go. A closed pre-alpha among friends, for now.","pre.btn":"🔔 Tell me when it openeth","pre.peek":"Behind the glass: the true board, alive. Each card is a coloured bar.","pre.peekFake":"Behind the glass: how a board at its labours doth appear.","pre.night":"🌙 The night watchman holdeth sway · 😴 the human doth rest","features.aria":"What it doth","f.pile.h":"One pile for thee","f.pile.html":"<b>For thee</b> holdeth all that awaiteth thee, across every project: questions, things to try, tasks that only a mortal may do. Thy queue telleth what cometh next and how long it taketh.","f.sleep.h":"Companies that labour whilst thou sleepest","f.sleep.p":"Each project hath a lead and a company of AI agents. Comment on a card and the company waketh, doth the work, and handeth it back with steps a weary mortal may follow.","f.tester.h":"An AI tester looketh first","f.tester.p":"Ere aught reacheth thee, a tester followeth the steps in a copy of the app and sheweth what it saw, with a screenshot. Flick through those that passed and accept in a click.","f.proof.h":"Proof, not promises","f.proof.p":"Every hand-over sheweth what changed: the files, the diff, the screenshots. No opening of every app to learn if it be done.","f.chat.h":"Parley with thy leads","f.chat.p":"A Discord-style rail: one icon per project, purple diamonds for what needeth thee. Send a lead an idea; he turneth it into cards and a plan, with a ✅ Go button.","f.tidy.h":"Keepeth itself tidy","f.tidy.p":"Kindred cards fold into one, muddled titles are mended, and a token check keepeth the code lean. Fewer things to switch betwixt, less to ponder.","f.private.h":"Thine, upon thy computer","f.private.li1":"The board runneth on thine own machine and answereth only thee.","f.private.li2":"Private missives betwixt people are end-to-end encrypted.","f.private.li3":"No accounts, no trackers, no cookies.","f.lang.h":"In thy tongue","f.lang.p":"Over 120 tongues, from Dutch, Welsh and Japanese to pirate, Yoda and Klingon, with a quick turn back to English for the jargon of the trade.","f.service.h":"From a notion to a true service","f.service.p":"Hast thou built aught with AI that folk now use? Mark it a service and the board helpeth thee keep it well: uptime checks, a public status page, incidents with a written account, changes that need a Go, backups checked daily. Help teacheth each step as thou goest.","msgr.h2":"AI-gile Messenger: thy company in thy pocket","msgr.p1":"Speak with thy AI company without opening the board. Converse with thy project leads and thy friends, and behold a card's test steps and answer them, all from thy phone.","msgr.p2":"To pair it, scan a QR code upon thy board. The first time? A friendly demo chat doth show thee around.","msgr.when":"Android first, then a web version for phones and iPhone.","msgr.who":"Thy project lead","msgr.b1":"The dark mode mending is ready. Wouldst thou have the test steps?","msgr.b2":"Aye, prithee!","msgr.b3":"1. Open Settings. 2. Pick Dark. Doth it look aright?","tl.aria":"Timeline from the first parley to the roadmap","tl.h2":"From the first parley to what cometh next","tl.lede":"True dates and hours, in thine own time zone. After this day it is the plan, with no dates promised.","tl.today":"This day","tl.planned":"planned","tl.doing":"afoot","tl.cards.one":"{n} card","tl.cards.other":"{n} cards","join.h2":"Join in","join.lede":"AI-gile is built by a bearded weird fellow with AuDHD and some few battles for his mind's health, and a great number of patient agents. It is private for now, in a closed alpha with friends. Wouldst thou have a go when it openeth?","join.btn":"Register interest","join.small":"We shall send thee a letter, naught else","footer.tag":"AI-gile. No trackers, no cookies, no stand-up coffee.","footer.licence":"Business licence","footer.status":"Status","footer.privacy":"What we keep","footer.thanks":"Calls by the grace of ChilledChat","form.sending":"Sending…","form.failed":"That availed not: try again anon.","form.offline":"Could not reach AI-gile: try again anon.","form.keep":"We use this but to answer thee, and then delete it. No trackers, no cookies.","form.keepLink":"What we keep","interest.title":"AI-gile: tell me when the alpha openeth","interest.description":"Leave thine email to hear when AI-gile's closed alpha or beta openeth.","interest.h1":"🔔 Tell me when it openeth","interest.lede":"AI-gile is in closed pre-alpha. Leave thine email and we shall write once, when there is a place for thee.","interest.email":"Thine email","interest.which":"Which test?","interest.alpha":"Closed alpha: early, rough, many changes","interest.beta":"Beta: steadier, later","interest.both":"Either, whichever cometh first","interest.submit":"Put me on the list","interest.thanks":"Thanks! Thou art on the list.","licence.title":"AI-gile: business licence","licence.description":"Usest thou AI-gile in thy business? Apply for a free business licence.","licence.h1":"📜 Business licence","licence.lede":"Usest thou AI-gile at work? Tell us who thou art and what thou dost. If it doth some good, the licence is free.","licence.company":"Company","licence.website":"Website","licence.what":"What thou dost","licence.how":"How it helpeth the world","licence.email":"Email","licence.submit":"Apply","licence.thanks":"Thanks! We shall reply by email.","status.title":"AI-gile status","status.h1":"AI-gile status","status.quiet":"All quiet","status.intro":"Doth AI-gile work at this hour? This page tryeth the website, board sharing, calls and the download every 5 minutes.","status.up":"Working (it answered in {ms} ms)","status.slow":"Answered not the last check; trying anew","status.down":"Down: it answered not the last two checks","status.svc.web":"Website","status.svc.web.offers":"This site: what AI-gile is, and the interest form","status.svc.boards":"Board sharing","status.svc.boards.offers":"Public boards, messages betwixt friends, and invites","status.svc.calls":"Calls","status.svc.calls.offers":"Voice, video and screen share within AI-gile","status.svc.download":"Download","status.svc.download.offers":"The Windows installer and invite links","status.checking":"Checking…","status.offline":"Cannot reach the status service this hour (retrying)","status.updated":"updated {ago}","status.justNow":"e'en now","status.min":"{n} min ago","status.hours":"{n} h ago","status.days":"{n} d ago","privacy.title":"AI-gile: what we keep","privacy.h1":"What we keep","privacy.lede":"In brief: only what thou sendest us, and not for long.","privacy.only":"Only what thou sendest us: what thou typest into a form, as thine email. Naught else of thee.","privacy.sealed":"It is sealed so our server cannot read it: in thy browser ere it leaveth (on an older browser, the moment it arriveth). Only our own board may open it.","privacy.server":"It is deleted from the server so soon as it reacheth our board. Aught still there after 30 days is deleted all the same.","privacy.board":"We keep it upon our board only till we have answered thee, then delete it there also.","privacy.none":"No trackers, no cookies, no analytics.","privacy.local":"Thy tongue and thy choice of light or dark abide in thine own browser. They are never sent to us.","privacy.ask":"Wouldst thou have it gone sooner? Answer our email and say so.","live.h2":"Behold it being built, alive","live.caption":"Each card is hid: thou seest the shape of the work, not the words.","live.watching.one":"alive: {n} beholding","live.watching.other":"alive: {n} beholding","live.last.now":"Last card moved but now","live.last.min.one":"Last card moved {n} minute ago","live.last.min.other":"Last card moved {n} minutes ago","live.last.hour.one":"Last card moved {n} hour ago","live.last.hour.other":"Last card moved {n} hours ago","live.last.day.one":"Last card moved {n} day ago","live.last.day.other":"Last card moved {n} days ago","live.offline":"The living board doth take a breath. Return anon, good friend.","live.cols":"Backlog|To be done|Afoot|The company doth review|For thee to test|For the company|Done"},"lines":{"unit":"words","sizes":[{"n":1,"texts":["Kanban.","Automatons.","Entrusted."]},{"n":2,"texts":["Robot kanban.","Agents, marshalled.","Ideas, wrought."]},{"n":3,"texts":["Kanban for automatons.","Ideas become deeds.","Free agent kanban."]},{"n":5,"texts":["A board whereon agents toil.","Thou writest cards. Agents build.","Free, local, proven, mildly daft."]},{"n":8,"texts":["A free kanban board where AI agents labour.","Write thine idea. Agents build it. Thou accepteth.","Agile for one mortal and many patient automatons."]},{"n":13,"texts":["A kanban board upon thy computer, where AI agents take up the cards.","Write an idea. A company of agents buildeth it. A tester proveth it.","Free, no accounts, no trackers: a board, some robots, and thou in command."]},{"n":21,"texts":["AI-gile is a kanban board for labouring with AI coding agents. They take up the cards; thou triest and acceptest them.","Each project hath a lead and a company of AI agents. Comment on any card and the company setteth to work.","A free, private to-do board that runneth on thine own computer. The labourers are robots. The one who saith yea is thee."]},{"n":34,"texts":["Thou placest ideas upon a board. A company of AI agents turneth them into working features, proveth them, and handeth them back with steps to try. Naught is done until thou sayest so.","AI-gile is a homespun kanban board that Rich built with much help from the very agents it now governeth. It is free, runneth on thy computer, and is shared with friends, not sold.","Picture a plain kanban board, with columns from Backlog to Done, save that AI agents take up the cards. They report their progress, ask when they stick, and ever await thy thumbs up."]},{"n":55,"texts":["AI-gile is a kanban board where the company is made of AI agents. Each project hath a lead who planneth the work and helpers who build it. When a feature is ready, an AI tester trieth it and taketh a screenshot, then it landeth in thy pile. Accept it, or comment and they rework it.","It began as one mortal's way of keeping watch over many AI coding sessions at once, and grew into a proper board. It runneth on thy machine, needeth no account, and hath no trackers. It is free for friends and the curious. It is also unfinished, so expect rough edges and the odd surprise.","Here is the honest tale. Thou must still have the ideas, and thou must still prove the results. What AI-gile doth is all that lieth betwixt: it keepeth the cards in order, waketh the right agent when thou commentest, sheweth exactly what changed, and gathereth all of it into one short pile for thee."]},{"n":89,"texts":["AI-gile is a free kanban board that thou runnest upon thine own computer. In place of folk, each project hath a company of AI agents: a lead who turneth thine ideas into cards and a plan, and helpers who take up the cards in order of weight. When a thing is built, an AI tester followeth the test steps and sheweth thee what it saw. Then it awaiteth in one pile named For thee. Thou acceptest it, or thou commentest and the company hath another go. Naught ever reacheth Done without thee.","Some things thou mightest not expect. A night watch keepeth the To do column filled whilst thou sleepest, choosing cards that need no answer from thee. A token counter sheweth how much the agents have spent this day and this week, and No Token Mode biddeth them cease their spending. Thou canst send missives to friends, and private missives are end-to-end encrypted. The board speaketh about 120 tongues, Dutch, Flemish, pirate and Klingon among them. None of it costeth a penny, and none is trying to sell it thee.","AI-gile is a small, personal undertaking, not a company. Rich desired to tend several AI coding projects without opening every app to look in on them, so he and the agents built a board for it, then used the board to build the rest of itself. It is in closed pre-alpha, which meaneth it worketh, mostly, for a handful of friends. There is no price page, no newsletter and no plan for growth. If it soundeth useful, thou mayest ask to try it when it openeth a little more."]},{"n":144,"texts":["AI-gile is a kanban board for one mortal and a great many AI agents. It runneth on thine own computer and is wholly free. Thou addest projects, and each project getteth a lead and a small company. Thou chattest with the lead, a little like Discord, and describest an idea; the lead turneth it into cards and a plan, then waiteth for thee to press Go. The company worketh through the cards in order of weight, using a plain command line made for language models. Ere aught cometh back to thee, an AI tester followeth the steps in a copy of the app and attacheth a screenshot. Finished work landeth in thy pile with the changed files and the diff. Thou acceptest it, or thou leavest a comment and the company waketh and tries again. Only thou canst move a card to Done.","A day with AI-gile, roughly. At eventide thou leavest a few comments: this button is in the wrong place, that list should be sorted, might we have a dark mode. Thou goest to bed. The agents read the comments, make the changes, prove them and hand them back to thee. If To do runneth dry, the night watch filleth it from the backlog with cards that need no answer from thee. At morn there is one short pile: a couple of questions and a few things to try, each with steps a sleepy mortal may follow and a screenshot of it working. Thou clickest through, acceptest the good ones and sendest back the rest. A token counter sheweth what it all spent, and No Token Mode is there for lean weeks. Then thou breakfastest, wherein the agents cannot yet help.","First, what AI-gile is not. It is not a startup, it is not for sale, and none is gathering thy data. It is a free board that runneth on thy computer, with no accounts, no trackers and no cookies. What it is: one tidy place to see every AI coding project at once, with a company of agents doing the cards and thee making the decisions. It foldeth related cards together, mendeth muddled titles, and keepeth watch that the code stay lean. It speaketh about 120 tongues, from Dutch and Flemish to pirate and Klingon. Friends may send each other missives, privately and encrypted. It was built by Rich and a great number of patient agents, mostly using itself. It is in closed pre-alpha, so it is rough in places. If it soundeth like merriment, ask kindly and thou mayest enter early."]}],"quips":{"1":"One word. Bold. Perchance too bold.","3":"Three words. Already more honest than most product pages.","8":"Eight words. Still shorter than a stand-up.","21":"The lengths are story points, by the way. Of course they are.","55":"Fifty-five words. Two cards were finished whilst thou readest.","144":"That is the long one. There is no 233. The agents have gone to bed."}},"timeline":{"first-idea.name":"The first idea","first-idea.line":"The very first parley, ere any code did exist.","first-board.name":"First board","first-board.line":"A board that keepeth tally of its own building: cards, columns, drag and drop, projects.","team-roles.name":"Company and roles","team-roles.line":"Agent profiles, company templates, spaces and who doth what.","install.name":"Install and releases","install.line":"A zip a friend may install, self-updates, channels and the rolling back.","usage-saver.name":"Usage saver","usage-saver.line":"Measure what runs cost, keep the code lean, spare thy limit.","friends.name":"Friends and sharing","friends.line":"Private missives, a scrambled relay, invites, roles and shared projects.","languages.name":"Tongues","languages.line":"Every screen text in a tongue file, with Dutch and Flemish first.","ai-tester.name":"AI tester","ai-tester.line":"A tester looketh over every hand-over first and sheweth what it saw.","website.name":"The website","website.line":"aigile.lol, the teaser and this timeline.","streaming.name":"Chat and streaming","streaming.line":"Discord, Twitch, OBS, streamer mode, GIFs and emojis.","no-ai.name":"No AI edition","no-ai.line":"A board for folk who code without AI, and public boards.","night-watch.name":"Night watch","night-watch.line":"A watchman and Scrum Master keep the companies at their task whilst thou sleepest.","p-more.name":"Everything else","p-more.line":"Smaller ideas still awaiting their turn.","p-android.name":"Phone and Android","p-android.line":"Reach thy board from a phone, then a native Android app.","p-release.name":"Alpha and beyond","p-release.line":"Closed alpha, the live site, then beta.","p-languages.name":"More tongues","p-languages.line":"130 tongues, and a mode of immersion for those that would learn.","p-engines.name":"More AI engines","p-engines.line":"Choose Claude, Codex, Gemini, Copilot or Cursor for each agent.","p-pro.name":"Pro practice","p-pro.line":"Risk labels, merge gates, incident cards and guard rails.","p-self.name":"Looking after thee","p-self.line":"Tired mode, self-care reminders and 4:20.","p-servers.name":"Servers and scale","p-servers.line":"Global server settings, roles and planning for growth.","p-livestream.name":"Streaming extras","p-livestream.line":"Twitch chat, custom emojis and a public live view."},"words":{"button":"📖 Jargon of the trade","h":"📖 Words made plain","intro":"Free training in plain language: every word thou meetest from a first idea to a service people rely upon, with Agile, building, keeping it safe and working with AI along the way.","search":"Seek a word…","none":"No word matcheth that.","close":"Close","count":{"one":"{count} word","other":"{count} words"},"groups":[{"id":"idea","name":"💡 Idea and discovery"},{"id":"plan","name":"🗺️ Planning the work"},{"id":"agile","name":"🔁 Agile ways of working"},{"id":"build","name":"🛠️ The building of it"},{"id":"test","name":"🧪 Testing and quality"},{"id":"change","name":"🔀 Changing it safely"},{"id":"run","name":"🛎️ The keeping of a service"},{"id":"sec","name":"🔒 Security and privacy"},{"id":"ai","name":"🤖 Working with AI"},{"id":"money","name":"💰 Coin and licences"}],"list":[{"id":"discovery","g":"idea","word":"Discovery","text":"The early stage of finding out which problem is worth the solving, and for whom, ere anything be built.","also":["discovery phase"]},{"id":"problemstmt","g":"idea","word":"Problem statement","text":"One or two sentences saying who hath a trouble, what it is and why it mattereth, so that all take aim at the same mark.","also":["problem statements"]},{"id":"user","g":"idea","word":"User","text":"A person who useth what thou buildest. His needs are what the work is for.","also":["users"],"noTip":1},{"id":"stakeholder","g":"idea","word":"Stakeholder","text":"Any who careth how the work turneth out or is touched by it, like those who pay for it, use it or uphold it.","also":["stakeholders"]},{"id":"persona","g":"idea","word":"Persona","text":"A made-up but lifelike person who standeth for one kind of user, so the team may ask \"would Sam find this easy?\"","also":["personas"]},{"id":"userresearch","g":"idea","word":"User research","text":"Speaking with and watching real people to learn what they need, rather than guessing.","also":["user interviews"]},{"id":"journey","g":"idea","word":"User journey","text":"The steps a person taketh to get a thing done, from first hearing of it to the finishing, also beyond thy product. Drawing it out showeth where they stick.","also":["user journeys","customer journey"]},{"id":"painpoint","g":"idea","word":"Pain point","text":"Something that vexeth or hindereth people today. Good products take pain points away.","also":["pain points"]},{"id":"assumption","g":"idea","word":"Assumption","text":"Something thou believest but hast not yet checked. Writing assumptions down showeth what to test first.","also":["assumptions"],"noTip":1},{"id":"hypothesis","g":"idea","word":"Hypothesis","text":"A best guess thou meanest to check, with what thou lookest to happen, like \"people will sign up if the first month be free\".","also":["hypotheses"]},{"id":"experiment","g":"idea","word":"Experiment","text":"A small planned trial to learn whether an idea worketh, ere thou stake much upon it.","also":["experiments"],"noTip":1},{"id":"poc","g":"idea","word":"Proof of concept (PoC)","text":"A quick rough try to see whether an idea can work at all. It is usually cast aside once thou hast the answer.","also":["PoC","proof of concept"]},{"id":"prototype","g":"idea","word":"Prototype","text":"An early model of the product, often pictures to click upon, to try the idea on people ere it be built aright.","also":["prototypes"]},{"id":"wireframe","g":"idea","word":"Wireframe","text":"A simple sketch of a screen showing where things go, without colours or true content.","also":["wireframes"]},{"id":"mockup","g":"idea","word":"Mockup","text":"A detailed picture of how a screen shall look, with true colours and text, but nothing yet worketh.","also":["mockups","mock-up","mock-ups"]},{"id":"bizcase","g":"idea","word":"Business case","text":"The reasons for doing a project: what it costeth, what it bringeth in or saveth, and the risks.","also":["business cases"]},{"id":"feasibility","g":"idea","word":"Feasibility","text":"Whether a thing can truly be built and kept with the time, coin and skills thou hast."},{"id":"outcome","g":"idea","word":"Outcome","text":"The change thou wouldst have for people, like fewer missed appointments. It mattereth more than how much thou buildest.","also":["outcomes"],"noTip":1},{"id":"output","g":"idea","word":"Output","text":"Something the team maketh, like a new screen or a report. The making of it helpeth no one of itself.","also":["outputs"],"noTip":1},{"id":"successmetric","g":"idea","word":"Success metric","text":"A number that telleth thee whether the work did what it was for, like more people finishing their order.","also":["success metrics"]},{"id":"kpi","g":"idea","word":"Key performance indicator (KPI)","text":"An important number thou watchest to see whether all goeth well, like sign-ups per week.","also":["KPI","KPIs","key performance indicator"]},{"id":"okr","g":"idea","word":"Objectives and key results (OKRs)","text":"A way of setting goals: the objective saith what thou wouldst have, and a few key results are the numbers that show thou hast come there.","also":["OKR","OKRs"]},{"id":"product","g":"plan","word":"Product","text":"The thing being built and kept for its users, such as an app, a website or a tool.","also":["products"],"noTip":1},{"id":"vision","g":"plan","word":"Product vision","text":"A short statement of whom the product helpeth and whither it heads in the long run.","also":["vision statement"]},{"id":"po","g":"plan","word":"Product owner (PO)","text":"The person who decideth what is built and in what order, so the team ever worketh on what mattereth most. In AI-gile that is thee.","also":["PO","product owners"]},{"id":"pm","g":"plan","word":"Product manager (PM)","text":"The person who looketh to a product's direction: which troubles it solveth, for whom and why. PM may also mean project manager, so check which.","also":["product managers"]},{"id":"projmgr","g":"plan","word":"Project manager","text":"The person who keepeth a project on time and within the purse, marking who doth what and by when.","also":["project managers"]},{"id":"roadmap","g":"plan","word":"Roadmap","text":"A rough plan of what cometh over the next months, in order. It showeth the road, not exact dates, and changeth as thou learnest.","also":["roadmaps"]},{"id":"milestone","g":"plan","word":"Milestone","text":"A point in a project worth the marking, like \"first version live\" or \"100 users\".","also":["milestones"]},{"id":"mvp","g":"plan","word":"Minimum viable product (MVP)","text":"The smallest version of a product that is yet useful to real people, so thou mayest learn from them betimes.","also":["MVP","MVPs","minimum viable product"]},{"id":"requirement","g":"plan","word":"Requirement","text":"Something the finished product must do or be.","also":["requirements"],"noTip":1},{"id":"scope","g":"plan","word":"Scope","text":"What is included in the work and, no less important, what is not.","also":["in scope","out of scope"]},{"id":"scopecreep","g":"plan","word":"Scope creep","text":"When more and more is added to the work bit by bit, with none agreeing the extra time or cost, so that it never quite endeth.","also":["feature creep"]},{"id":"feature","g":"plan","word":"Feature","text":"One thing the product can do for people, like \"reset thy password\".","also":["features"],"noTip":1},{"id":"epic","g":"plan","word":"Epic","text":"A great piece of work, too large for one go, so it is split into smaller cards.","also":["epics"]},{"id":"story","g":"plan","word":"User story","text":"A small piece of work written from the user's side: \"As a shopper, I want to save my basket, so I may finish later.\" It beginneth a conversation about what to build.","also":["user stories"]},{"id":"ac","g":"plan","word":"Acceptance criteria (AC)","text":"The checks one card must pass to count as done, agreed ere work beginneth, like \"the basket is still there after I log out and in again\".","also":["acceptance criteria"]},{"id":"task","g":"plan","word":"Task","text":"A single job to be done, often one small step of a greater story.","also":["tasks"],"noTip":1},{"id":"ticket","g":"plan","word":"Ticket","text":"Another word for a card: one piece of work or one request, tracked from start to finish.","also":["tickets"]},{"id":"priority","g":"plan","word":"Priority","text":"How important or urgent a thing is against all the rest, so the most important work goeth first.","also":["priorities"],"noTip":1},{"id":"prioritise","g":"plan","word":"Prioritisation","text":"Putting work in order of importance. A common way is MoSCoW: Must have, Should have, Could have, Won't have this time.","also":["MoSCoW"]},{"id":"estimate","g":"plan","word":"Estimate","text":"A best guess at how great or how long a piece of work is. It is a guess, not a promise.","also":["estimates","estimation"],"noTip":1},{"id":"storypoints","g":"plan","word":"Story points","text":"A way of guessing the size of work by comparing cards one with another (\"about twice as large as that one\") rather than in hours. They are not for comparing teams.","also":["story point"]},{"id":"tshirt","g":"plan","word":"T-shirt sizing","text":"Guessing the size of work as S, M, L or XL. Quick, and good enough for early planning.","also":["t-shirt sizes"]},{"id":"poker","g":"plan","word":"Planning poker","text":"A game for estimating: all show a size card at the same moment, then the highest and lowest tell why.","also":["Scrum poker"]},{"id":"dependency","g":"plan","word":"Dependency","text":"When one piece of work cannot start or finish until another doth.","also":["dependencies"]},{"id":"blocker","g":"plan","word":"Blocker","text":"Anything staying work from moving forward this moment, like a missing answer or a broken tool.","also":["blockers"]},{"id":"deadline","g":"plan","word":"Deadline","text":"The date by which a thing must be finished.","also":["deadlines"],"noTip":1},{"id":"deliverable","g":"plan","word":"Deliverable","text":"Something solid the work yieldeth and handeth over, like a working page or a report.","also":["deliverables"]},{"id":"forecast","g":"plan","word":"Forecast","text":"A prophecy of what is likely to happen, like when the work shall be done, based on what thou knowest so far.","also":["forecasts"],"noTip":1},{"id":"metric","g":"plan","word":"Metric","text":"Anything thou measurest and trackest over time, like page visits or how long a fix taketh.","also":["metrics"]},{"id":"feedback","g":"plan","word":"Feedback","text":"What people tell thee of thy work, good and ill. To have it early and often is the heart of Agile.","noTip":1},{"id":"backlog","g":"agile","word":"Backlog","text":"The waiting list of ideas and work not yet planned in, with the most important at the top. Nothing there is worked upon till it moveth to To be done."},{"id":"sprint","g":"agile","word":"Sprint","text":"A short, fixed stretch of work (often one or two weeks, never more than a month) with a goal and an agreed set of cards to finish.","also":["sprints"]},{"id":"standup","g":"agile","word":"Stand-up","text":"A quick daily check-in: what each team member did, what he doth next, and what stayeth him. In Scrum it is called the daily scrum.","also":["standup","stand-ups","daily scrum","daily stand-up"]},{"id":"kanban","g":"agile","word":"Kanban","text":"A way of working where cards move across a board's columns (like To do, In progress, Done) and the team limiteth how much is in progress at once, so work keepeth flowing."},{"id":"wip","g":"agile","word":"WIP limit","text":"WIP is short for work in progress. A WIP limit is the most cards a column should hold at once, so the team finisheth things ere it start more.","also":["WIP"]},{"id":"dod","g":"agile","word":"Definition of Done","text":"The team’s short checklist of what “finished” meaneth, as tested and explained, ere a card be handed thee. Its twin, the Definition of Ready, saith when a card is clear enough to begin.","also":["Definition of Ready","DoD","DoR"]},{"id":"retro","g":"agile","word":"Retro","text":"A regular look back at how the team worketh, to agree on one or two things to do better the next time. Short for retrospective. In AI-gile a retro suggesteth a change to the team's ways of working, and thou sayest Go or Not yet.","also":["retros","retrospective","retrospectives"]},{"id":"swarm","g":"agile","word":"Swarm","text":"All hands on deck: many people drop other work to mend one urgent thing together till it be sorted. In AI-gile every team helpeth on one project, and other projects wait meanwhile.","also":["swarming"]},{"id":"scrummaster","g":"agile","word":"Scrum Master","text":"In Scrum, the person who helpeth the team work well: clearing what blocketh them, keeping meetings on track and coaching good habits, without bossing any. In AI-gile the Lead Scrum Master spieth stuck cards, nudgeth the teams and remindeth thee of what is waiting, across every project.","also":["Chief Scrum Master","Lead Scrum Master"]},{"id":"agile","g":"agile","word":"Agile","text":"A way of working in small steps: build a little, show real results often, learn from what people say and change the plan as thou goest, rather than planning all up front.","also":["Agile development","agile ways of working"]},{"id":"manifesto","g":"agile","word":"Agile Manifesto","text":"A short statement written in 2001 by makers of software. It setteth people, working results, close work with customers and answering to change above heavy plans and paperwork.","also":["Manifesto for Agile Software Development"]},{"id":"waterfall","g":"agile","word":"Waterfall","text":"The older way of working: plan all, then build it all, then test it all, one stage after another. Changes late on are hard and costly.","also":["waterfall model"]},{"id":"iteration","g":"agile","word":"Iteration","text":"One round of building something, checking it and mending it. Agile work is a chain of these, and a sprint is one kind.","also":["iterations"]},{"id":"increment","g":"agile","word":"Increment","text":"A new working piece added to the product in a sprint or round of work, which fitteth with what was there before.","also":["increments"]},{"id":"scrum","g":"agile","word":"Scrum","text":"A popular Agile way of working: a small team worketh in short sprints toward a goal, with set roles and a few regular meetings to plan, check and mend."},{"id":"scrumteam","g":"agile","word":"Scrum team","text":"The small company that doth the work in Scrum: a product owner, a Scrum Master and the developers.","also":["Scrum teams"]},{"id":"ceremonies","g":"agile","word":"Scrum events","text":"The regular meetings in Scrum: sprint planning, the daily scrum, the sprint review and the retro. Many call them ceremonies.","also":["ceremonies","Scrum ceremonies"]},{"id":"sprintplan","g":"agile","word":"Sprint planning","text":"The meeting at the start of a sprint where the team agreeth why the sprint mattereth, which cards to take on and how to begin.","also":["planning meeting"]},{"id":"sprintgoal","g":"agile","word":"Sprint goal","text":"One sentence saying what a sprint is for. Small tasks may change by the way, so long as the goal be met.","also":["sprint goals"]},{"id":"sprintbacklog","g":"agile","word":"Sprint backlog","text":"The cards picked for the present sprint, with the team's plan for doing them.","also":["sprint backlogs"]},{"id":"productbacklog","g":"agile","word":"Product backlog","text":"The whole ordered list of all that might be built for the product, the most important at the top. It keepeth changing as thou learnest.","also":["product backlogs"]},{"id":"productgoal","g":"agile","word":"Product goal","text":"The greater result the product worketh toward, which helpeth the team choose what to do next.","also":["product goals"]},{"id":"refinement","g":"agile","word":"Backlog refinement","text":"Going through the backlog at regular times to tidy, split, order and add detail to cards, so they be ready to take up. Also called backlog grooming.","also":["backlog grooming","refinement"]},{"id":"sprintreview","g":"agile","word":"Sprint review","text":"A meeting at the end of a sprint where the team showeth what it finished and heareth what people think, to decide what cometh next.","also":["sprint reviews"]},{"id":"demo","g":"agile","word":"Demo","text":"Showing finished work working, live, to those who asked for it.","also":["demos"],"noTip":1},{"id":"timebox","g":"agile","word":"Timebox","text":"A fixed measure of time for something. When it runneth out thou stoppest, even if not all be done.","also":["timeboxed","timeboxes"]},{"id":"velocity","g":"agile","word":"Velocity","text":"How much work a team usually finisheth in a sprint, used to plan how much to take on the next time. It is no score of how hard folk labour.","also":["team velocity"]},{"id":"capacity","g":"agile","word":"Capacity","text":"How much work the team can take on in a season, after holidays and other tasks.","noTip":1},{"id":"burndown","g":"agile","word":"Burndown chart","text":"A chart of the work left in a sprint falling day by day. If the line lieth flat, something is stuck.","also":["burndown","burn-down chart"]},{"id":"burnup","g":"agile","word":"Burnup chart","text":"A chart of finished work rising over time, beside the total planned, so thou mayest see when thou shalt arrive.","also":["burnup","burn-up chart"]},{"id":"kanbanboard","g":"agile","word":"Kanban board","text":"The board itself: a column for each stage of the work, with cards moving across.","also":["Kanban boards"]},{"id":"pullsys","g":"agile","word":"Pull system","text":"A way of working where new work beginneth only when someone hath room to take it on, rather than being pushed upon a full plate.","also":["pull-based"]},{"id":"flow","g":"agile","word":"Flow","text":"How smoothly work moveth across the board. Good flow meaneth cards keep moving rather than piling up.","also":["flow of work"],"noTip":1},{"id":"leadtime","g":"agile","word":"Lead time","text":"How long it taketh from someone asking for a thing to its being finished.","also":["lead times"]},{"id":"cycletime","g":"agile","word":"Cycle time","text":"How long a card taketh from when work truly beginneth upon it to when it is finished.","also":["cycle times"]},{"id":"throughput","g":"agile","word":"Throughput","text":"How many cards get finished in a week, or in any set time.","also":["throughput rate"]},{"id":"bottleneck","g":"agile","word":"Bottleneck","text":"The one stage where work pileth up and hindereth all behind it, like the narrow neck of a bottle.","also":["bottlenecks"]},{"id":"swimlane","g":"agile","word":"Swimlane","text":"A row across the board that gathereth cards of one kind, such as urgent work or one team's cards.","also":["swimlanes","swim lane"]},{"id":"lean","g":"agile","word":"Lean","text":"A way of working that cutteth out waste (anything that helpeth not the customer) and keepeth work flowing."},{"id":"waste","g":"agile","word":"Waste","text":"In Lean, anything that taketh effort but helpeth not the customer, like waiting, rework or building things none useth.","noTip":1},{"id":"kaizen","g":"agile","word":"Continuous improvement","text":"Getting a little better all the time through small regular changes, then checking they helped. Retros are one way to do it. Also called kaizen.","also":["kaizen"]},{"id":"selforg","g":"agile","word":"Self-organising team","text":"A team that decideth for itself how to do the work, rather than being told step by step.","also":["self-organising","self-managing team"]},{"id":"crossfunc","g":"agile","word":"Cross-functional team","text":"A team that hath all the skills it needeth to finish the work itself, like design, building and testing.","also":["cross-functional"]},{"id":"spike","g":"agile","word":"Spike","text":"A short, timeboxed bit of research to answer a question ere thou commit to the true work.","also":["spikes"]},{"id":"rework","g":"agile","word":"Rework","text":"Doing work again because it was not right the first time.","also":["reworked"]},{"id":"safe","g":"agile","word":"Scaled Agile (SAFe)","text":"Ways of using Agile across many teams in a great organisation. SAFe (the Scaled Agile Framework) is one well known example.","also":["scaled Agile"]},{"id":"repo","g":"build","word":"Repo","text":"The project's folder of code with its full history of commits. It may live on thy computer, on GitHub, or both.","also":["repository"]},{"id":"branch","g":"build","word":"Branch","text":"A separate line of work in the code, so changes may be made without touching the main version.","also":["branches"]},{"id":"commit","g":"build","word":"Commit","text":"A saved snapshot of the code, with a short note of what changed. Thou canst ever return to one.","also":["commits"]},{"id":"push","g":"build","word":"Push","text":"Sending thy saved snapshots (commits) from this computer to the shared copy online, such as GitHub, so they be backed up and others may get them."},{"id":"merge","g":"build","word":"Merge","text":"Joining the changes from one branch into another, usually back into the main version."},{"id":"pr","g":"build","word":"Pull request","text":"Asking for a branch's changes to be checked and merged into the main version. Some sites call it a merge request.","also":["PR","PRs","merge request"]},{"id":"refactor","g":"build","word":"Refactor","text":"Tidying the code without changing what it doth: smaller files, clearer names, less repetition."},{"id":"bug","g":"build","word":"Bug","text":"Something that worketh not as it should.","also":["bugs"]},{"id":"peerreview","g":"build","word":"Peer review","text":"A second pair of eyes: someone other than the author checketh the work ere it reacheth thee, so fewer mistakes pass through. In AI-gile another AI checketh each card.","also":["code review"]},{"id":"code","g":"build","word":"Code","text":"The written instructions that tell a computer what to do. Also called source code.","also":["source code"],"noTip":1},{"id":"proglang","g":"build","word":"Programming language","text":"A tongue for writing code, such as JavaScript, Python or Java. Different ones suit different tasks.","also":["programming languages"]},{"id":"developer","g":"build","word":"Developer (dev)","text":"Someone who writeth and changeth code. Also called a programmer or software engineer.","also":["developer","developers","programmer","programmers","software engineer"]},{"id":"software","g":"build","word":"Software","text":"Programs that run on computers and phones, as opposed to the machines themselves (the hardware).","noTip":1},{"id":"app","g":"build","word":"App","text":"Short for application: a program people use to get a thing done, on a phone, a computer or in a web browser.","also":["apps","application","applications"],"noTip":1},{"id":"webapp","g":"build","word":"Web app","text":"An app that runneth in a web browser, so there is nothing to install.","also":["web apps","web application"]},{"id":"frontend","g":"build","word":"Front end","text":"The part of an app thou seest and clickest upon: the screens, buttons and words, often in thy browser.","also":["front-end","frontend"]},{"id":"backend","g":"build","word":"Back end","text":"The behind-the-scenes part of an app that keepeth the data and doth the work when thou clickest something, like checking thy password.","also":["back-end","backend"]},{"id":"fullstack","g":"build","word":"Full stack","text":"Working upon both the front end and the back end.","also":["full-stack"]},{"id":"ui","g":"build","word":"User interface (UI)","text":"What a person seeth and useth on screen: layout, buttons, menus and text.","also":["UI","user interface"]},{"id":"ux","g":"build","word":"User experience (UX)","text":"How it feeleth to use something: easy, clear and pleasant, or confusing and slow.","also":["UX","user experience"]},{"id":"accessibility","g":"build","word":"Accessibility (a11y)","text":"Making things usable by all, including people who cannot see well, cannot use a mouse or use a screen reader.","also":["a11y"]},{"id":"responsive","g":"build","word":"Responsive design","text":"Making pages fit and work well on any screen size, from a phone to a great monitor."},{"id":"designsys","g":"build","word":"Design system","text":"A shared kit of colours, fonts, buttons and rules, so every screen looketh and behaveth the same way.","also":["design systems"]},{"id":"architecture","g":"build","word":"Architecture","text":"The whole shape of a system: what the main parts are and how they speak one with another."},{"id":"database","g":"build","word":"Database (DB)","text":"An orderly store of information, like a very mighty spreadsheet that the app can read and change.","also":["database","databases","DB"]},{"id":"schema","g":"build","word":"Database schema","text":"The layout of a database: which tables of information it hath and what goeth in each.","also":["schema"]},{"id":"sql","g":"build","word":"SQL","text":"Short for structured query language: the tongue used to ask many databases for information or to change it.","also":["Structured Query Language"]},{"id":"data","g":"build","word":"Data","text":"Information kept by a computer, like names, orders or settings.","also":["dataset","datasets"],"noTip":1},{"id":"server","g":"build","word":"Server","text":"A computer that is ever on and answereth requests from other computers, like sending a web page when thou visitest it.","also":["servers"]},{"id":"client","g":"build","word":"Client","text":"The side that asketh for something, usually thy browser or app, speaking to a server. In business it also meaneth just a customer.","also":["clients"],"noTip":1},{"id":"api","g":"build","word":"API","text":"Short for application programming interface: a set menu of requests one program may make of another, like asking a weather service for today's forecast.","also":["APIs","application programming interface"]},{"id":"endpoint","g":"build","word":"Endpoint","text":"One item on an API's menu: a web address a program can call to get or send something.","also":["endpoints"]},{"id":"integration","g":"build","word":"Integration","text":"Joining two systems so they work together, like thy shop sending orders to thy accounts software.","also":["integrations"]},{"id":"webhook","g":"build","word":"Webhook","text":"A message one system sendeth to another of itself the moment something happeneth, like \"payment received\".","also":["webhooks"]},{"id":"library","g":"build","word":"Library","text":"Ready-made code someone else wrote that thou mayest reuse instead of writing it thyself.","also":["libraries"],"noTip":1},{"id":"framework","g":"build","word":"Framework","text":"A ready-made structure for building an app that decideth much of how the code is laid out, like a house frame thou fillest in.","also":["frameworks"]},{"id":"sdk","g":"build","word":"Software development kit (SDK)","text":"A box of tools, code and examples for building software for one platform or service.","also":["SDK","SDKs"]},{"id":"softdep","g":"build","word":"Software dependency","text":"A library or tool thy code needeth to work. Keeping them up to date mattereth for safety.","also":["software dependencies"]},{"id":"package","g":"build","word":"Package","text":"A bundle of ready-made code thou canst install and use in a project.","also":["packages"],"noTip":1},{"id":"pkgmgr","g":"build","word":"Package manager","text":"A tool that fetcheth and updateth the packages thy code dependeth on. npm is a common one.","also":["package managers","npm"]},{"id":"git","g":"build","word":"Git","text":"The most widely used tool for keeping the history of code changes, as commits and branches."},{"id":"github","g":"build","word":"GitHub","text":"A website that keepeth Git repos online, so teams may share code, review changes and track work."},{"id":"vcs","g":"build","word":"Version control","text":"Keeping a full history of every change to the files, so thou mayest see who changed what and go back if need be. Git doth this.","also":["source control","version control system"]},{"id":"clone","g":"build","word":"Clone","text":"Making thine own full copy of a repo, with its history, upon thy computer.","also":["cloned","cloning"]},{"id":"pull","g":"build","word":"Pull","text":"Fetching the latest commits from the shared copy (like GitHub) onto thy computer. The opposite of push.","also":["git pull"],"noTip":1},{"id":"mainbranch","g":"build","word":"Main branch","text":"The official version of the code that all work from, often called main or master.","also":["master branch"]},{"id":"conflict","g":"build","word":"Merge conflict","text":"When two changes touch the same lines in different ways, so the computer cannot join them and a person must choose.","also":["merge conflicts"]},{"id":"diff","g":"build","word":"Diff","text":"A view showing exactly what changed between two versions: lines added and lines taken away.","also":["diffs"]},{"id":"fork","g":"build","word":"Fork","text":"Thine own copy of another's repo, which thou mayest change without touching his.","also":["forks","forked"]},{"id":"script","g":"build","word":"Script","text":"A short program that doth one task of itself, like tidying files or starting the app.","also":["scripts"],"noTip":1},{"id":"build","g":"build","word":"Build","text":"Turning the code into something ready to run, or the ready-to-run result itself.","also":["builds"],"noTip":1},{"id":"compile","g":"build","word":"Compile","text":"Translating code that people wrote into a form the computer can run directly.","also":["compiler"]},{"id":"cli","g":"build","word":"Command line (CLI)","text":"A text window where thou typest instructions for the computer instead of clicking. Also called the terminal.","also":["command line","command-line","CLI","terminal"]},{"id":"config","g":"build","word":"Configuration (config)","text":"The settings that rule how software behaveth, kept apart from the code so they be easy to change.","also":["config","configuration"],"noTip":1},{"id":"envvar","g":"build","word":"Environment variable","text":"A setting handed to a program when it startheth, often used for addresses or passwords so they be not written into the code.","also":["environment variables","env var"]},{"id":"debugging","g":"build","word":"Debugging","text":"Hunting down why something worketh not, and mending it.","also":["debug","debugged"]},{"id":"pairing","g":"build","word":"Pair programming","text":"Two people (or a person and an AI) working on the same code together, one typing and one checking.","also":["pairing"]},{"id":"docs","g":"build","word":"Documentation (docs)","text":"Written explanations of how something worketh or how to use it.","also":["documentation","docs"],"noTip":1},{"id":"readme","g":"build","word":"README","text":"The first file to read in a repo: what the project is and how to get it running.","also":["READMEs"]},{"id":"legacy","g":"build","word":"Legacy system","text":"An older system still in use that is hard to change, often because few yet understand it.","also":["legacy systems","legacy code"]},{"id":"techdebt","g":"build","word":"Technical debt","text":"Shortcuts that save time now but make later changes slower, like a loan that gathereth interest. Refactoring payeth it down.","also":["tech debt"]},{"id":"test","g":"test","word":"Test","text":"A check that something worketh the way it should. Some tests the computer runneth of itself every time the code changeth; others are thee trying a finished card ere thou accept it.","also":["tests"],"noTip":1},{"id":"qa","g":"test","word":"QA","text":"Short for quality assurance: all that is done to make sure work is right ere it goeth live. In AI-gile that meaneth the automatic checks: when QA is red, something failed, and it cannot go live till that be mended.","also":["quality checks","quality assurance"]},{"id":"testpile","g":"test","word":"Heap of trials","text":"The finished cards awaiting thy trial, one after another. Accept one or send it back with a note, and the next cometh up.","also":["test pile","test piles","heaps of trials"]},{"id":"autotest","g":"test","word":"Automated test","text":"A check the computer runneth of itself every time the code changeth, to catch mistakes betimes.","also":["automated tests","automatic tests"]},{"id":"manualtest","g":"test","word":"Manual test","text":"A person trying the work by hand to see whether it behaveth as it should.","also":["manual tests","manual testing"]},{"id":"unittest","g":"test","word":"Unit test","text":"A small automatic check of one tiny piece of code upon its own.","also":["unit tests"]},{"id":"integtest","g":"test","word":"Integration test","text":"A check that several parts work rightly together, not just one at a time.","also":["integration tests"]},{"id":"endtoend","g":"test","word":"End-to-end test (E2E)","text":"A test that acteth like a real user from start to finish, such as signing up, buying and paying.","also":["E2E","end-to-end tests"]},{"id":"uat","g":"test","word":"User acceptance testing (UAT)","text":"Those who asked for the work try it themselves and say whether it doth what they need. AI-gile's test pile is its version of this.","also":["UAT","acceptance testing"]},{"id":"regression","g":"test","word":"Regression","text":"Something that used to work but broke after a change. Regression tests check that the old things yet work.","also":["regressions","regression test","regression tests","regression testing"]},{"id":"smoke","g":"test","word":"Smoke test","text":"A very quick check that the main things work at all, for example right after a change goeth live. If it fail, stop and look.","also":["smoke tests"]},{"id":"exploratory","g":"test","word":"Exploratory testing","text":"Trying the product freely and poking at it in diverse ways, to find troubles that planned checks would miss.","also":["exploratory test","exploratory tests"]},{"id":"testcase","g":"test","word":"Test case","text":"One written scenario to try: the steps, and what should happen.","also":["test cases"]},{"id":"coverage","g":"test","word":"Test coverage","text":"How much of the code is checked by automatic tests. More is usually safer, but high coverage alone proveth not that it worketh well.","also":["code coverage"]},{"id":"testdata","g":"test","word":"Test data","text":"Made-up example information used while testing, so no real person's private matters be exposed.","also":["test fixtures"]},{"id":"edgecase","g":"test","word":"Edge case","text":"An unusual case at the limits, like an empty form or a name with an apostrophe, where things oft break.","also":["edge cases"]},{"id":"happypath","g":"test","word":"Happy path","text":"The ordinary road where all goeth right. Good testing also trieth the unhappy paths."},{"id":"perftest","g":"test","word":"Performance testing","text":"Checking how fast something is and how well it copeth under strain.","also":["performance test","performance tests"]},{"id":"loadtest","g":"test","word":"Load testing","text":"Checking how a system copeth when many people use it at once.","also":["load test","load tests"]},{"id":"sectest","g":"test","word":"Security testing","text":"Looking for weaknesses that might let someone misuse a system or see what he should not.","also":["security test","security tests"]},{"id":"accesstest","g":"test","word":"Accessibility testing","text":"Checking that people of different abilities can use the product, including with a screen reader or only a keyboard.","also":["accessibility test"]},{"id":"linting","g":"test","word":"Linting","text":"An automatic check that spotteth likely mistakes and untidy style in code, like a spelling checker for programs.","also":["linter","lint"]},{"id":"static","g":"test","word":"Static analysis","text":"Checking code for troubles by reading it automatically, without running it.","also":["static code analysis"]},{"id":"flaky","g":"test","word":"Flaky test","text":"A test that sometimes passeth and sometimes faileth for no clear reason, so it cannot be fully trusted.","also":["flaky tests"]},{"id":"repro","g":"test","word":"Reproduce (repro)","text":"Making a bug happen again on purpose by following the same steps, so it may be studied and mended. Writing those steps down is the most useful part of a bug report.","also":["repro","reproduce","steps to reproduce"]},{"id":"severity","g":"test","word":"Severity","text":"How grave a problem's effect is, from a small vexation to everything stopping.","also":["severity level"]},{"id":"deploy","g":"change","word":"Deploy","text":"Copying a new version of the software onto the computers that run it, such as a test copy or the live service."},{"id":"release","g":"change","word":"Release","text":"A named bundle of finished work that goeth live together, with short notes of what hath changed. 🚀 Releases writeth the notes from the cards that are done.","also":["releases"]},{"id":"rollback","g":"change","word":"Roll back","text":"Going back to the last version that worked when a new one causeth trouble. In AI-gile, Roll back gathereth the undo steps written on each change into one checklist.","also":["rollback","roll-back","rolled back"]},{"id":"live","g":"change","word":"Live","text":"The true version that folk do use, as against a copy for trying things. Developers call it also production.","also":["production"],"noTip":1},{"id":"change","g":"change","word":"Change","text":"A planned change to aught that folk rely upon, written down first: what, wherefore, the risk, when, and how to undo it. Begin one with 🔀 Raise a change.","also":["change request","change requests"],"noTip":1},{"id":"risk","g":"change","word":"Risk","text":"Something that might go amiss, scored by how likely and how grievous it would be. ⚠️ Risks keepeth them in one list, highest score first, each with a day to look again.","also":["risks","risk register"]},{"id":"chgwin","g":"change","word":"Change window","text":"The hours when changes may go live, such as a quiet Tuesday evening. Outside a window a change card may not be finished, unless it be an emergency.","also":["change windows"]},{"id":"gonogo","g":"change","word":"Go / no go","text":"A last check just ere a change goeth live: each person who must approve saith Go or No go. It goeth ahead only when all say Go.","also":["go/no go","go-no-go"]},{"id":"approval","g":"change","word":"Approval","text":"Awaiting a yea ere work beginneth. A card a friend raiseth, or a change, waiteth in ✅ Approvals till thou approvest or declinest it.","also":["approvals"]},{"id":"quiettime","g":"change","word":"Quiet time","text":"A stretch of time, like during a live stream, a demo or overnight, when nothing goeth live. The teams keep working and testing, but going live waiteth till it endeth. Elsewhere it is called a change freeze.","also":["quiet times","change freeze"]},{"id":"devops","g":"change","word":"DevOps","text":"A way of working where those who build software and those who run it work as one team, with much automation, so changes go live often and safely."},{"id":"cicd","g":"change","word":"CI/CD (continuous integration and delivery)","text":"All men's changes are joined into the main version often and checked automatically each time (continuous integration), so the software is ever ready to go live at the press of a button (continuous delivery).","also":["CI/CD","CI","CD","continuous integration","continuous delivery"]},{"id":"contdeploy","g":"change","word":"Continuous deployment","text":"One step beyond continuous delivery: every change that passeth the checks goeth live of itself, with no button to press.","also":["continuous deployments"]},{"id":"pipeline","g":"change","word":"Pipeline","text":"The automatic series of steps a change goeth through on its way to live, like build, test, then deploy.","also":["pipelines"]},{"id":"environment","g":"change","word":"Environment","text":"One separate copy of the system for one purpose, such as one to build in, one to test in and the live one.","also":["environments"],"noTip":1},{"id":"devenv","g":"change","word":"Development environment","text":"The copy a developer worketh in, often upon his own computer, where breaking things harmeth none.","also":["dev environment"]},{"id":"testenv","g":"change","word":"Test environment","text":"A separate copy of the system used just for testing, so the real service be not touched.","also":["test environments"]},{"id":"staging","g":"change","word":"Staging","text":"A last copy set up just like live, for a final check ere a change goeth live.","also":["staging environment"]},{"id":"artifact","g":"change","word":"Build artifact","text":"The file or bundle a build produceth, ready to be stored, checked or put live.","also":["build artifacts"]},{"id":"hotfix","g":"change","word":"Hotfix","text":"An urgent fix put live quickly, outside the usual plan, because something important is broken.","also":["hotfixes"]},{"id":"patch","g":"change","word":"Patch","text":"A small update that mendeth a bug or closeth a security hole. Applying security patches quickly mattereth.","also":["patches","security patch","security patches"]},{"id":"version","g":"change","word":"Version number","text":"A label like 2.4.1 that saith which release thou hast. Often the first number changeth for great changes and the last for small fixes.","also":["version numbers","semantic versioning"]},{"id":"relnotes","g":"change","word":"Release notes","text":"A short plain list of what changed in a release, for those who use it, including fixes and known limits. Also called a changelog.","also":["changelog","change log"]},{"id":"flag","g":"change","word":"Feature flag","text":"An on and off switch for a feature, so new work may go live hidden and be turned on (or off again) without a new release.","also":["feature flags","feature toggle","feature toggles"]},{"id":"rollfwd","g":"change","word":"Roll forward","text":"Mending a bad release by quickly putting out a new, corrected version instead of going back to the old one.","also":["rolling forward","rolled forward"]},{"id":"canary","g":"change","word":"Canary release","text":"Putting a change live for a small company first, and for all only once it looketh fine. Named after the canaries miners took underground as an early warning.","also":["canary releases","canary"]},{"id":"bluegreen","g":"change","word":"Blue-green deployment","text":"Keeping two copies of the live system and switching people over to the new one in one go, so thou canst switch straight back if it go ill.","also":["blue-green","blue green deployment"]},{"id":"zerodown","g":"change","word":"Zero-downtime deployment","text":"Putting a new version live without the service ever stopping for its users.","also":["zero downtime","zero-downtime"]},{"id":"chgenable","g":"change","word":"Change enablement","text":"Helping changes to succeed: weighing the risk, getting the right approval and picking a good hour. Also called change management.","also":["change management"]},{"id":"cab","g":"change","word":"Change advisory board (CAB)","text":"A company that looketh over important changes and agreeth whether and when they may go ahead.","also":["CAB"]},{"id":"stdchange","g":"change","word":"Standard change","text":"A low-risk change done the same tried and tested way each time, so it is approved beforehand.","also":["standard changes"]},{"id":"normchange","g":"change","word":"Normal change","text":"A change that needeth to be checked and approved ere it goeth ahead.","also":["normal changes"]},{"id":"emergchange","g":"change","word":"Emergency change","text":"A change that must happen right away to mend or prevent grave trouble, with a quicker approval to match.","also":["emergency changes"]},{"id":"automation","g":"change","word":"Automation","text":"Getting the computer to do a repeated task of itself, so it is quicker and done the same way every time.","also":["automated"],"noTip":1},{"id":"infra","g":"change","word":"Infrastructure","text":"The machines, networks and services that software runneth upon.","also":["infra"]},{"id":"iac","g":"change","word":"Infrastructure as code (IaC)","text":"Describing thy servers and settings in files kept with the code, so they may be rebuilt exactly the same way every time.","also":["IaC"]},{"id":"cloud","g":"change","word":"Cloud","text":"Renting computers, storage and services from a great provider over the internet, instead of owning the machines thyself.","also":["the cloud","cloud computing"]},{"id":"provider","g":"change","word":"Cloud provider","text":"A company that rentheth out computing over the internet, such as Amazon Web Services (AWS), Microsoft Azure or Google Cloud.","also":["cloud providers"]},{"id":"hosting","g":"change","word":"Hosting","text":"Where thy app or website liveth and runneth so people can reach it, usually rented from a company."},{"id":"domain","g":"change","word":"Domain name","text":"The web address people type, like example.com. Thou rentest it by the year, so it must be renewed.","also":["domain names","domain"]},{"id":"dns","g":"change","word":"DNS","text":"Short for domain name system: the internet's book of addresses, which turneth a name like example.com into the address of the right computer.","also":["domain name system"]},{"id":"container","g":"change","word":"Container","text":"A sealed package holding an app and all it needeth, so it runneth the same on any computer. Docker is the best known tool.","also":["containers","Docker"],"noTip":1},{"id":"vm","g":"change","word":"Virtual machine (VM)","text":"A pretend computer running inside a real one, so one great machine may act as many.","also":["VM","VMs","virtual machines"]},{"id":"serverless","g":"change","word":"Serverless","text":"Running code without tending any servers thyself: the provider runneth it when needed and thou payest for what thou usest."},{"id":"lb","g":"change","word":"Load balancer","text":"Something that spreadeth visitors across several servers, so that no single one be overwhelmed.","also":["load balancers"]},{"id":"cache","g":"change","word":"Cache","text":"A handy store of recent results kept close by, so the same thing need not be fetched or worked out again. Clearing it can mend pages that look out of date.","also":["caches","caching","cached"]},{"id":"cdn","g":"change","word":"Content delivery network (CDN)","text":"A worldwide set of servers holding copies of thy pages and pictures near thy visitors, so they load quickly.","also":["CDN"]},{"id":"migration","g":"change","word":"Migration","text":"Moving data or systems from an old setup to a new one, or carefully changing how a database is laid out.","also":["migrations","database migration"]},{"id":"service","g":"run","word":"Service","text":"Something thou hast built that folk rely upon, as a website or an app, tended so it keepeth working. Tick “This project is a service” and say what it offereth, who useth it and who is on call.","also":["services"]},{"id":"uptimepct","g":"run","word":"Uptime","text":"How much of the time a service is working, usually as a percentage. 99.9% yet alloweth about 43 minutes down a month.","also":["uptime percentage"]},{"id":"uptime","g":"run","word":"Uptime check","text":"A check that runneth of itself every few minutes, to see thy service yet answereth. If it faileth several times together, AI-gile openeth an incident card of its own accord.","also":["uptime checks"]},{"id":"statuspage","g":"run","word":"Status page","text":"A public page that showeth whether a service worketh (green, orange or red) with the latest tidings, so they that use it may look instead of asking.","also":["status pages"]},{"id":"desk","g":"run","word":"Service desk","text":"Whither come the questions and reports of those that use thy service. AI-gile sorteth each into a request, an incident or a notion, and saith so when it seemeth a thing already reported.","also":["service desks","help desk","helpdesk"]},{"id":"svcrequest","g":"run","word":"Service request","text":"One asking for some common thing, as a new account or a little help, rather than reporting that aught is broken. It awaiteth its turn; an incident goeth first.","also":["service requests"]},{"id":"incident","g":"run","word":"Incident","text":"Something that is broken or not working properly for those using it right now, like the website being down or very slow. A 🔥 incident card leapeth the queue: getting it working again cometh first.","also":["incidents"]},{"id":"major","g":"run","word":"Grave mischance","text":"A great incident: many folk afflicted, or coin or data in peril. One button setteth every team upon it (swarm), rouseth whoever is on call and asketh a status line every thirty minutes.","also":["major incident","major incidents","grave mischances"]},{"id":"oncall","g":"run","word":"On call","text":"Being the one who answereth when aught breaketh, even by night. Each service hath an on-call team member who is roused first for its incidents.","also":["on-call"]},{"id":"replyby","g":"run","word":"Time of answer","text":"How long a card may wait for a first answer, as an hour for an incident. Thereafter it beareth a red clock, so naught is quietly forgot. Called also a response target.","also":["times of answer","reply-by time","reply-by times","response target"]},{"id":"postmortem","g":"run","word":"Post-mortem","text":"A short look back after an incident: what befell, what helped and what to change, blaming no one. An incident may not be closed without one.","also":["post-mortems","postmortem","post-incident review"]},{"id":"problem","g":"run","word":"Problem","text":"The hidden cause behind one incident or more. A 🧩 problem card gathereth incidents that keep returning, so the cause be found and mended for good.","also":["problems"],"noTip":1},{"id":"rootcause","g":"run","word":"Root cause","text":"The true reason a thing broke, not merely what thou sawest go amiss. Mend the root cause and the incident returneth no more.","also":["root causes"]},{"id":"workaround","g":"run","word":"Workaround","text":"A way to keep things working till the true mending be ready, as restarting a thing when it sticketh. 'Tis written upon the problem card, so none need puzzle it out again.","also":["workarounds"]},{"id":"knownerror","g":"run","word":"Known folly","text":"A problem whose cause is understood but is not yet mended, usually with a workaround written down. 🧩 Known errors listeth them, so all use the workaround instead of digging again.","also":["known follies","known error","known errors"]},{"id":"runbook","g":"run","word":"Runbook","text":"Instructions step by step for mending a known kind of trouble, that it be done the same way, swiftly, every time. After a grave mischance the team may propose one for thee to OK.","also":["runbooks"]},{"id":"ci","g":"run","word":"Configuration item","text":"One thing whereon thy service doth depend, as a server, a domain, a certificate, a key or a purveyor. 🗂️ Configuration items listeth them for each service, that thou mayst see what a mischance doth touch and what wanteth renewing or a backup.","also":["configuration items"]},{"id":"expiry","g":"run","word":"Expiry date","text":"The date something ceaseth to work unless it be renewed, like a website's security certificate or its web address. AI-gile watcheth these dates and maketh one card to renew each one 30 days before, so nothing stoppeth by surprise.","also":["expiry dates","expiry","expiry watch"]},{"id":"backup","g":"run","word":"Backup","text":"A saved copy of thy data from before, to fall back upon if aught be lost or marred. AI-gile maketh a backup of thy boards every day.","also":["backups","back-up","back-ups"]},{"id":"restore","g":"run","word":"Restore","text":"Putting data back from a backup. A backup truly counteth only once thou knowest it can be restored, so 'tis worth the trying now and then.","also":["restored"]},{"id":"svcreview","g":"run","word":"Service review","text":"A look back upon one month of a service: incidents opened and mended, how swiftly folk had answer, uptime and tokens spent. The Monthly review showeth it for each service.","also":["service reviews","monthly review","monthly reviews"]},{"id":"accessreview","g":"run","word":"Review of access","text":"Checking every 90 days who can still get in: share links, friends' roles and saved passwords and keys. Thou keepest or removest each one, so old access lingereth not.","also":["access review","access reviews","reviews of access"]},{"id":"improvements","g":"run","word":"List of betterments","text":"All that the team resolved to do better, in one place: retro counsels, review actions and mendings of trouble, each with its status. Seek it under 📈 Betterments.","also":["improvement list","improvements","betterments","lists of betterments"]},{"id":"tokencap","g":"run","word":"Token cap","text":"A monthly bound upon the tokens a service’s agents may spend. At 80% thou art warned; at 100% their labour in the background waiteth till next month, or till thou raise the cap.","also":["token caps"]},{"id":"svcmgmt","g":"run","word":"Service management","text":"All that is needed to keep a service useful and working for those who rely upon it, day after day."},{"id":"itil","g":"run","word":"ITIL","text":"A widely used guide to good service management, covering things like incidents, problems and changes. The name once stood for IT Infrastructure Library."},{"id":"itsm","g":"run","word":"IT service management (ITSM)","text":"Running technology as a service for people, with clear ways to handle requests, incidents, changes and improvements.","also":["ITSM"]},{"id":"managed","g":"run","word":"Managed service","text":"A service that another runneth and looketh to for thee, under an agreement about how well it must work.","also":["managed services"]},{"id":"svcowner","g":"run","word":"Service owner","text":"The person who answereth for a service as a whole: how well it worketh, what it costeth and how it improveth.","also":["service owners"]},{"id":"sla","g":"run","word":"Service level agreement (SLA)","text":"A written promise to customers of how well a service shall work, like \"up 99.9% of the time\" or \"answered within an hour\", often with coin returned if it be broken.","also":["SLA","SLAs","service level agreement"]},{"id":"slo","g":"run","word":"Service level objective (SLO)","text":"The team's own target for how well a service should work over a season, usually set a little stricter than the SLA to be safe.","also":["SLO","SLOs"]},{"id":"sli","g":"run","word":"Service level indicator (SLI)","text":"The actual measurement thou checkest against a target, like the share of visits that loaded fine.","also":["SLI","SLIs"]},{"id":"availability","g":"run","word":"Availability","text":"Whether people can use a service when they have need, often measured as uptime.","also":["high availability"]},{"id":"downtime","g":"run","word":"Downtime","text":"Time when a service worketh not or is switched off, planned or not.","also":["down time"]},{"id":"errorbudget","g":"run","word":"Error budget","text":"The small amount of failure thy reliability target alloweth. While some is left thou mayest take risks with changes; once it is spent, thou slowest.","also":["error budgets"]},{"id":"outage","g":"run","word":"Outage","text":"A time when a service is down or badly broken for its users.","also":["outages"]},{"id":"degraded","g":"run","word":"Degraded","text":"Working, but ill: slow, or with some parts not working.","also":["degraded service"]},{"id":"monitoring","g":"run","word":"Monitoring","text":"Watching a service automatically all the time, so troubles are spied, ideally ere users notice."},{"id":"observability","g":"run","word":"Observability","text":"How well thou canst tell what passeth within a system from the outside, using its logs, numbers and traces.","also":["o11y"]},{"id":"log","g":"run","word":"Log","text":"A running diary a program keepeth of what it doth, used to work out what went amiss.","also":["logs","logging"],"noTip":1},{"id":"trace","g":"run","word":"Trace","text":"A record of how one request travelleth through the diverse parts of a system, step by step, showing where it slowed.","also":["traces","tracing"]},{"id":"latency","g":"run","word":"Latency","text":"How long something taketh to answer, like the wait between clicking and the page appearing."},{"id":"alert","g":"run","word":"Alert","text":"An automatic message that something needeth attention, like the website not answering.","also":["alerts","alerting"],"noTip":1},{"id":"alertfatigue","g":"run","word":"Alert fatigue","text":"When there be so many alerts that people begin to ignore them, the important ones too.","also":["alarm fatigue"]},{"id":"dashboard","g":"run","word":"Dashboard","text":"A screen showing the most important numbers and statuses at a glance.","also":["dashboards"],"noTip":1},{"id":"paging","g":"run","word":"Paging","text":"Urgently calling or waking the on-call person about a problem.","also":["paged"]},{"id":"escalation","g":"run","word":"Escalation","text":"Bringing in one of more skill or authority when an issue cannot be sorted at the present level, or not fast enough.","also":["escalate","escalated"]},{"id":"triage","g":"run","word":"Triage","text":"Quickly sorting incoming issues by how urgent and important they be, so the worst is handled first.","also":["triaged"]},{"id":"impact","g":"run","word":"Impact","text":"How much something toucheth people: how many, and how sorely.","noTip":1},{"id":"urgency","g":"run","word":"Urgency","text":"How quickly something must be dealt with. Impact and urgency together set the priority.","noTip":1},{"id":"plevels","g":"run","word":"Priority levels (P1, P2…)","text":"Labels for how urgent an issue is. P1 is the gravest and needeth action straightway.","also":["P1","P2","P3","P4"]},{"id":"queue","g":"run","word":"Ticket queue","text":"The list of requests and incidents waiting to be taken up.","also":["ticket queues"]},{"id":"tiers","g":"run","word":"First line and second line","text":"Levels of support: first line taketh the call and mendeth simple things; second line hath deeper skills for harder ones. Also called tier 1 and tier 2.","also":["first-line support","tier 1","tier 2"]},{"id":"ic","g":"run","word":"Incident commander","text":"The one person who leadeth the response to an incident, so all know who decideth and who doth what.","also":["incident commanders"]},{"id":"responsetime","g":"run","word":"Response time","text":"How long it taketh ere someone first taketh up a request or incident.","also":["response times"]},{"id":"resolution","g":"run","word":"Resolution time","text":"How long it taketh to sort out a request or incident fully, from report to mended.","also":["resolution times","time to resolve"]},{"id":"mttr","g":"run","word":"Mean time to recover (MTTR)","text":"On average, how long it taketh to get a service working again after it breaketh. MTTR can mean slightly different things, so say what thou measurest.","also":["MTTR","mean time to restore"]},{"id":"mtbf","g":"run","word":"Mean time between failures (MTBF)","text":"On average, how long a service runneth before something breaketh.","also":["MTBF"]},{"id":"cmdb","g":"run","word":"Configuration management database (CMDB)","text":"The list of all thy configuration items and how they connect, so thou mayest see what dependeth on what.","also":["CMDB"]},{"id":"asset","g":"run","word":"Asset","text":"Anything of value thou ownest or payest for to run the service, like a laptop, a software licence or a domain.","also":["assets"],"noTip":1},{"id":"capplan","g":"run","word":"Capacity planning","text":"Making sure there shall be enough computer power, storage and people for what is coming.","also":["capacity plan"]},{"id":"scaling","g":"run","word":"Scaling","text":"Coping with more users by giving a machine more power (scaling up) or adding more machines (scaling out).","also":["scale up","scale out","scaling up","scaling out"]},{"id":"bcp","g":"run","word":"Business continuity","text":"Plans for keeping the important things going when something great goeth wrong, like losing an office, a key supplier or the computers.","also":["business continuity plan"]},{"id":"dr","g":"run","word":"Disaster recovery (DR)","text":"The plan and tools for getting a service back after something grave, like losing a whole data centre.","also":["disaster recovery"]},{"id":"rto","g":"run","word":"Recovery time objective (RTO)","text":"The longest a service may be down after a disaster ere it must be working again.","also":["RTO"]},{"id":"rpo","g":"run","word":"Recovery point objective (RPO)","text":"How much recent data thou couldst afford to lose, measured in time. An RPO of one hour meaneth backups at least every hour.","also":["RPO"]},{"id":"redundancy","g":"run","word":"Redundancy","text":"Having spares ready, like a second server, so one failure stoppeth not the service."},{"id":"failover","g":"run","word":"Failover","text":"Switching over to a spare system of itself when the usual one faileth.","also":["fail over"]},{"id":"spof","g":"run","word":"Single point of failure","text":"One part that bringeth all down with it when it breaketh, because there is no spare.","also":["single points of failure","SPOF"]},{"id":"maintwin","g":"run","word":"Maintenance window","text":"A planned time when a service may be paused or slow for upkeep, announced to users beforehand.","also":["maintenance windows","planned maintenance"]},{"id":"handover","g":"run","word":"Handover","text":"Passing work, knowledge and responsibility to another person or team, so nothing be dropped.","also":["handovers"]},{"id":"kb","g":"run","word":"Knowledge base","text":"A collection of help articles and answers, for users and for the team.","also":["knowledge bases"]},{"id":"csat","g":"run","word":"Customer satisfaction (CSAT)","text":"A score from users saying how glad they were, often asked after a request is closed.","also":["CSAT"]},{"id":"supplier","g":"run","word":"Supplier","text":"An outside company thou reliest upon, like thy hosting provider. Also called a vendor or third party.","also":["suppliers","vendor","vendors","third party"],"noTip":1},{"id":"retire","g":"run","word":"Service retirement","text":"Switching a service off for good, safely: telling its users, dealing with its data and access, and stopping its costs.","also":["retiring a service"]},{"id":"eol","g":"run","word":"End of life (EOL)","text":"When a product ceaseth to get updates or support from its maker, so it should be replaced.","also":["EOL","end-of-life"]},{"id":"cybersec","g":"sec","word":"Cybersecurity","text":"Protecting systems and data from being broken into, stolen or damaged.","also":["cyber security"]},{"id":"authn","g":"sec","word":"Authentication","text":"Checking who someone is, usually with a password or a code. Often shortened to authn.","also":["authn"]},{"id":"authz","g":"sec","word":"Authorisation","text":"Checking what someone is allowed to do once thou knowest who he is. Often shortened to authz.","also":["authz","authorization"]},{"id":"mfa","g":"sec","word":"Multi-factor authentication (MFA)","text":"Logging in with two or more proofs, like a password plus a code upon thy phone. Also called two-factor (2FA).","also":["MFA","2FA","two-factor","two-factor authentication"]},{"id":"sso","g":"sec","word":"Single sign-on (SSO)","text":"Logging in once to get into many systems, like using thy work account everywhere.","also":["SSO"]},{"id":"pwmgr","g":"sec","word":"Password manager","text":"An app that createth strong passwords and remembereth them for thee.","also":["password managers"]},{"id":"secret","g":"sec","word":"Secret","text":"A password, key or other private code a program useth to get into something. It must never be shared or written into the code.","also":["secrets"],"noTip":1},{"id":"apikey","g":"sec","word":"API key","text":"A secret code that letteth a program use another service's API, and showeth who useth (and payeth for) it.","also":["API keys"]},{"id":"accesstoken","g":"sec","word":"Access token","text":"A temporary pass that proveth a program is allowed in, so it needeth not thy password each time. Not the same as an AI token.","also":["access tokens"]},{"id":"encryption","g":"sec","word":"Encryption","text":"Scrambling information so that only one with the right key can read it.","also":["encrypted","encrypt"]},{"id":"https","g":"sec","word":"HTTPS","text":"The secure way web pages travel, shown by the padlock in thy browser, so that none in between can read or change them."},{"id":"cert","g":"sec","word":"SSL/TLS certificate","text":"A digital ID card that letteth a website prove who it is and use HTTPS. It expireth, so it must be renewed.","also":["TLS certificate","SSL certificate","certificate","certificates"]},{"id":"permissions","g":"sec","word":"Permissions","text":"The rules for who may see or change what.","also":["permission"],"noTip":1},{"id":"leastpriv","g":"sec","word":"Least privilege","text":"Giving each person or program only the access he truly needeth, for only as long as he needeth it.","also":["principle of least privilege"]},{"id":"rbac","g":"sec","word":"Role-based access control (RBAC)","text":"Giving access by role, like viewer or editor, rather than person by person.","also":["RBAC","role-based access"]},{"id":"vuln","g":"sec","word":"Vulnerability","text":"A weakness that someone could use to break in or cause harm.","also":["vulnerabilities"]},{"id":"zeroday","g":"sec","word":"Zero-day","text":"A weakness attackers know of ere the makers have had any time to mend it.","also":["zero-days","zero day"]},{"id":"malware","g":"sec","word":"Malware","text":"Harmful software, like viruses, made to damage, spy or steal."},{"id":"ransomware","g":"sec","word":"Ransomware","text":"Malware that locketh up thy files and demandeth coin to unlock them. Good backups are the best defence.","also":["ransomware attack"]},{"id":"phishing","g":"sec","word":"Phishing","text":"False messages that try to trick thee into giving away passwords or coin, or opening something harmful.","also":["phishing email","phishing emails"]},{"id":"socialeng","g":"sec","word":"Social engineering","text":"Tricking people, rather than computers, into giving access, like a false call from \"IT support\"."},{"id":"firewall","g":"sec","word":"Firewall","text":"A guard that decideth which network traffic may come in or go out.","also":["firewalls"]},{"id":"vpn","g":"sec","word":"VPN","text":"Short for virtual private network: a private, scrambled link over the internet, often used to reach work systems safely.","also":["virtual private network"]},{"id":"ddos","g":"sec","word":"Denial of service (DoS, DDoS)","text":"Flooding a service with so much false traffic that real people cannot use it. DDoS meaneth it cometh from many computers at once.","also":["DoS","DDoS","denial of service","DDoS attack"]},{"id":"pentest","g":"sec","word":"Penetration test (pen test)","text":"Hiring friendly experts to try to break in, so weaknesses are found ere real attackers find them.","also":["pen test","pen testing","penetration testing","pentest"]},{"id":"audit","g":"sec","word":"Security audit","text":"A careful check of how well something is protected, against a list of good practice.","also":["security audits"]},{"id":"threatmodel","g":"sec","word":"Threat modelling","text":"Thinking through who might attack something, how, and what thou wouldst do to stop them.","also":["threat model","threat modeling"]},{"id":"breach","g":"sec","word":"Data breach","text":"When private information getteth out to those who should not have it, or is lost or changed without leave.","also":["data breaches"]},{"id":"pii","g":"sec","word":"Personal data","text":"Any information about a person who can be identified, like a name, email address or place. Also called PII.","also":["PII","personally identifiable information"]},{"id":"gdpr","g":"sec","word":"GDPR","text":"The European law on personal data (the UK hath its own version): gather only what thou needest, keep it safe, and let people see or delete theirs.","also":["General Data Protection Regulation"]},{"id":"dataprot","g":"sec","word":"Data protection","text":"Looking after personal data properly and within the law.","also":["data protection law"]},{"id":"privacypolicy","g":"sec","word":"Privacy policy","text":"A public page saying what personal data thou gatherest, why, and what thou doest with it.","also":["privacy statement","privacy notice"]},{"id":"consent","g":"sec","word":"Consent","text":"A person's clear, free yes to his data being used in a particular way. He may take it back at any time.","also":["opt-in"],"noTip":1},{"id":"cookie","g":"sec","word":"Cookie","text":"A small file a website saveth in thy browser to remember things, like being logged in. Some need thy consent first.","also":["cookies"],"noTip":1},{"id":"minimisation","g":"sec","word":"Data minimisation","text":"Gathering and keeping only the personal data thou truly needest for the task.","also":["data minimization"]},{"id":"retention","g":"sec","word":"Data retention","text":"How long data is kept ere it be deleted. Keeping it no longer than needed is safer and often the law.","also":["retention period"]},{"id":"anon","g":"sec","word":"Anonymisation","text":"Changing data so that none can reasonably be identified from it any more.","also":["anonymised","anonymization","anonymous data"]},{"id":"pseudo","g":"sec","word":"Pseudonymisation","text":"Swapping names and other details for codes, with a key kept apart to link them back. It is still personal data.","also":["pseudonymised","pseudonymization"]},{"id":"dpa","g":"sec","word":"Data processing agreement (DPA)","text":"A contract saying how a supplier may handle personal data on thy behalf.","also":["DPA"]},{"id":"dpia","g":"sec","word":"Data protection impact assessment (DPIA)","text":"A careful look, ere thou begin, at how a plan to use personal data could touch people and how to lower the risks.","also":["DPIA"]},{"id":"auditlog","g":"sec","word":"Audit log","text":"A record of who did what and when, so actions may be checked hereafter.","also":["audit logs","audit trail"]},{"id":"compliance","g":"sec","word":"Compliance","text":"Following the laws, rules and standards that apply to thee, and being able to show that thou doest.","also":["compliant"]},{"id":"iso","g":"sec","word":"ISO 27001","text":"A well known international standard for managing information security. Companies may be certified against it.","also":["ISO/IEC 27001"]},{"id":"soc","g":"sec","word":"SOC 2","text":"A US report, checked by outside auditors, showing that a company looketh to customer data properly.","also":["SOC2"]},{"id":"agent","g":"ai","word":"Agent","text":"An AI that worketh on a task by itself: readeth the code, maketh changes, runneth checks and reporteth back. Its work still getteth checked.","also":["agents"]},{"id":"token","g":"ai","word":"Token","text":"The small pieces of text an AI readeth and writeth, about three quarters of a word each. AI use is counted in tokens, so fewer tokens leave more of thy plan.","also":["tokens"]},{"id":"hook","g":"ai","word":"Hook","text":"A small command that runneth of itself at a set moment, for example when an AI session startheth, so the team heareth thy comments.","also":["hooks"]},{"id":"ai","g":"ai","word":"Artificial intelligence (AI)","text":"Computer systems that do things we usually think need a person, like writing, answering questions or recognising pictures.","also":["AI","artificial intelligence"],"noTip":1},{"id":"ml","g":"ai","word":"Machine learning (ML)","text":"A way of making computers learn patterns from many examples, instead of giving them exact rules.","also":["machine learning"]},{"id":"model","g":"ai","word":"Model","text":"The trained \"brain\" of an AI system, built by learning from vast numbers of examples. Models differ in skill, speed and price.","also":["models","AI model"],"noTip":1},{"id":"llm","g":"ai","word":"Large language model (LLM)","text":"An AI model trained on vast amounts of text, so that it can read and write language.","also":["LLM","LLMs"]},{"id":"genai","g":"ai","word":"Generative AI","text":"AI that createth new things, like text, pictures or code, rather than only sorting or spotting them.","also":["GenAI"]},{"id":"chatbot","g":"ai","word":"Chatbot","text":"A program thou speakest with in everyday language, by typing or speaking.","also":["chatbots"]},{"id":"prompt","g":"ai","word":"Prompt","text":"What thou givest an AI: thy question or instructions, plus anything thou handest it. Clearer prompts usually get better answers.","also":["prompts"]},{"id":"prompteng","g":"ai","word":"Prompt engineering","text":"The skill of writing prompts that get reliable, useful results."},{"id":"sysprompt","g":"ai","word":"System prompt","text":"Background instructions an AI getteth ere the conversation beginneth, setting its role and rules. They weigh more than what thou typest.","also":["system prompts","system instruction","system instructions"]},{"id":"context","g":"ai","word":"Context","text":"All that the AI can see while it worketh: the instructions, thy messages, files it hath read and earlier replies.","noTip":1},{"id":"ctxwin","g":"ai","word":"Context window","text":"How much an AI can keep in mind at once, measured in tokens. Past that, older parts get dropped or summarised.","also":["context windows"]},{"id":"session","g":"ai","word":"Session","text":"One working conversation with an AI, from start to finish. A new session beginneth with a fresh memory.","also":["sessions"],"noTip":1},{"id":"memory","g":"ai","word":"Memory","text":"Notes an AI keepeth between sessions, so it remembereth thy preferences and past decisions.","noTip":1},{"id":"hallucination","g":"ai","word":"Hallucination","text":"When an AI saith something that soundeth sure of itself but is made up or wrong. Check important facts.","also":["hallucinations","hallucinate","hallucinates"]},{"id":"training","g":"ai","word":"Training","text":"Teaching a model by showing it vast numbers of examples, ere any use it.","also":["trained"],"noTip":1},{"id":"trainingdata","g":"ai","word":"Training data","text":"The examples a model learned from. Its knowledge stoppeth at the date that data was gathered.","also":["training set"]},{"id":"cutoff","g":"ai","word":"Knowledge cutoff","text":"The date an AI's built-in knowledge endeth. It knoweth not of later things unless it looketh them up.","also":["training cutoff"]},{"id":"finetune","g":"ai","word":"Fine-tuning","text":"Extra training of an existing model on thine own examples, to make it better at one particular task.","also":["fine-tune","fine-tuned","fine tuning"]},{"id":"inference","g":"ai","word":"Inference","text":"An AI model actually being used to answer something, as opposed to being trained.","also":["model inference"]},{"id":"tooluse","g":"ai","word":"Tool use","text":"An AI being able to do things, not just talk: run commands, read files or search the web, through tools the app giveth it.","also":["tool calling","tool call","tool calls"]},{"id":"subagent","g":"ai","word":"Subagent","text":"A helper AI to whom a main AI handeth a smaller task, and getteth the result back.","also":["subagents","sub-agent"]},{"id":"multiagent","g":"ai","word":"Multi-agent","text":"Several AIs working together on one piece of work, each with its own part, like a small team.","also":["multi-agent system"]},{"id":"autonomy","g":"ai","word":"Autonomy","text":"How much an AI may do on its own ere it must ask a person.","also":["autonomous"]},{"id":"hitl","g":"ai","word":"Human in the loop","text":"Keeping a person involved to check or approve what the AI doth at key points. In AI-gile that is thee.","also":["human-in-the-loop","HITL"]},{"id":"guardrails","g":"ai","word":"Guardrails","text":"Limits and checks that keep an AI's actions safe, like needing approval ere anything goeth live. They lower the risk of mistakes, but rule them not out.","also":["guardrail"]},{"id":"rag","g":"ai","word":"Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG)","text":"Letting an AI look things up in thine own documents ere it answereth, so its answers rest on thy facts.","also":["RAG","retrieval augmented generation"]},{"id":"embedding","g":"ai","word":"Embedding","text":"Turning text into a list of numbers that catcheth its meaning, so a computer may find things that mean the like.","also":["embeddings"]},{"id":"vectordb","g":"ai","word":"Vector database","text":"A database built to search those lists of numbers (embeddings), to find matter of a like meaning.","also":["vector databases","vector store"]},{"id":"mcp","g":"ai","word":"Model Context Protocol (MCP)","text":"A common way to plug tools and data sources into AI apps, so that an AI may use them.","also":["MCP"]},{"id":"temperature","g":"ai","word":"Temperature","text":"A setting for how adventurous an AI's answers be. Low giveth steadier, more foreseeable answers; high giveth more varied ones. Neither maketh it always right.","also":["model temperature"],"noTip":1},{"id":"multimodal","g":"ai","word":"Multimodal","text":"Able to work with more than one kind of information, such as text, pictures and sound.","also":["multi-modal"]},{"id":"evals","g":"ai","word":"Evaluation (eval)","text":"A planned test of how well an AI doth on chosen examples, so thou canst compare models or prompts.","also":["eval","evals"]},{"id":"bias","g":"ai","word":"Bias","text":"When an AI (or a person) leaneth unfairly one way, often because of what it learned from.","also":["biased"],"noTip":1},{"id":"responsible","g":"ai","word":"Responsible AI","text":"Using AI fairly, safely and honestly, with people still answerable for the results.","also":["ethical AI"]},{"id":"injection","g":"ai","word":"Prompt injection","text":"A trick where hidden instructions in a web page or file try to make an AI do something its user did not ask for.","also":["prompt injections"]},{"id":"ratelimit","g":"ai","word":"Rate limit","text":"A cap on how many requests thou mayest send to a service in a set time. Go over it and thou must wait.","also":["rate limits","rate limited"]},{"id":"usagelimit","g":"ai","word":"Usage limit","text":"How much AI work thy plan alloweth in a season, after which it pauseth or costeth more.","also":["usage limits"]},{"id":"vibe","g":"ai","word":"Vibe coding","text":"Building software mostly by describing what thou wouldst have to an AI and letting it write the code.","also":["vibe-coding"]},{"id":"budget","g":"money","word":"Budget","text":"The sum of coin set aside for something.","also":["budgets"],"noTip":1},{"id":"costest","g":"money","word":"Cost estimate","text":"A best guess at what something shall cost ere thou begin.","also":["cost estimates"]},{"id":"roi","g":"money","word":"Return on investment (ROI)","text":"What thou gettest back compared with what thou puttest in. If it be positive, it was worth it.","also":["ROI"]},{"id":"tco","g":"money","word":"Total cost of ownership (TCO)","text":"All that something truly costeth over its whole life, not just the price to buy it: running, support, upgrades and at last retiring it.","also":["TCO"]},{"id":"capex","g":"money","word":"CapEx and OpEx","text":"CapEx is coin spent up front on things thou keepest; OpEx is ongoing spending, like monthly bills.","also":["CapEx","OpEx","capital expenditure","operating expenditure"]},{"id":"subscription","g":"money","word":"Subscription","text":"Paying regularly, usually monthly or yearly, to keep using something.","also":["subscriptions"],"noTip":1},{"id":"saas","g":"money","word":"Software as a service (SaaS)","text":"Software thou usest online and payest for by subscription, while the maker runneth it for thee.","also":["SaaS"]},{"id":"payg","g":"money","word":"Pay as you go","text":"Paying only for what thou usest, like cloud computing or AI tokens.","also":["pay-as-you-go","usage-based pricing"]},{"id":"overage","g":"money","word":"Overage","text":"Use above what thy plan includeth, which can cost extra.","also":["overages","overage charges"]},{"id":"billingalert","g":"money","word":"Billing alert","text":"A message when spending or use reacheth a level thou hast chosen. It warneth thee, but stoppeth not always further charges.","also":["billing alerts","spending alert"]},{"id":"freetier","g":"money","word":"Free tier","text":"A free level of a paid service, with limits. Handy for starting out.","also":["free plan"]},{"id":"pricing","g":"money","word":"Pricing plan","text":"The diverse packages a service selleth, each with its own price and limits.","also":["pricing plans","price plan"]},{"id":"licence","g":"money","word":"Licence","text":"The rules for how thou mayest use, copy, change or share something another made, such as software, fonts or pictures.","also":["licences","license","licenses"],"noTip":1},{"id":"opensource","g":"money","word":"Open source","text":"Software whose code any may read, use and often change for free, under the rules of its licence.","also":["open-source","open source software","OSS"]},{"id":"osslicence","g":"money","word":"Open source licence","text":"The rules that come with open source code. Some let thee do almost anything (like MIT); some ask thee to share thy changes too (like GPL).","also":["open source licences","MIT licence","GPL"]},{"id":"proprietary","g":"money","word":"Proprietary","text":"Owned by a company and not free to copy or change. The opposite of open source.","also":["proprietary software"]},{"id":"copyright","g":"money","word":"Copyright","text":"The legal right of a creator to rule over copies of his work, including code and writing.","also":["copyrighted"],"noTip":1},{"id":"ip","g":"money","word":"Intellectual property (IP)","text":"Ideas and creations the law treateth as owned, like code, designs, names and logos.","also":["intellectual property"]},{"id":"tos","g":"money","word":"Terms of service","text":"The rules thou agreest to when thou usest a service.","also":["terms and conditions","terms of use"]},{"id":"contract","g":"money","word":"Contract","text":"A written agreement between two sides that the law shall back up.","also":["contracts"],"noTip":1},{"id":"sow","g":"money","word":"Statement of work (SOW)","text":"A document setting out exactly what work shall be done, by when and for how much.","also":["SOW"]},{"id":"fixedprice","g":"money","word":"Fixed price","text":"An agreed price for the whole task, however long it taketh.","also":["fixed-price"]},{"id":"tm","g":"money","word":"Time and materials","text":"Paying for the hours truly worked and the things truly used, rather than a set price.","also":["T&M"]},{"id":"invoice","g":"money","word":"Invoice","text":"A bill asking for payment for work done or goods supplied.","also":["invoices"],"noTip":1},{"id":"lockin","g":"money","word":"Vendor lock-in","text":"When moving away from a supplier is so hard or costly that thou art stuck with him.","also":["lock-in"]},{"id":"procurement","g":"money","word":"Procurement","text":"The process of choosing and buying from suppliers."},{"id":"servicecredit","g":"money","word":"Service credit","text":"Coin back or a discount thou gettest when a supplier misseth its SLA.","also":["service credits"]}]}};
